  "description": "Empirical test of conj:depth-stratified-frobenius-reciprocity at k=3 with candidate distinguished knots {4_1, 5_2, 6_1} via Wenzl embedding into H_{3A}. TWO ARMS, reported side by side (owner ruling 2026-09-05, bean qou-oots). PRIMARY / CANONICAL: the Molien weight f^lam*q^{-kappa}*d_q/[n]_q!, which is the unique corpus numerator normalised by an IDENTITY rather than by division (Lean molienSum_eq_qFactorial, sorry-free, all n and all q>1), whose kappa exponent is FORCED up to conjugation, and which IS the literature's q-Plancherel measure M_{n,q^2} (exact over every partition of n<=9), so Feray-Meliot's asymptotics apply to it and to nothing else here. SECOND ARM, labelled not fallback: d_q^2/D^2 (self-normalized, Reshetikhin-Turaev / Verlinde). WHY BOTH: the R1/R2/R3 requirement set does NOT separate them -- R2 asks only that the normaliser be n-independent and both satisfy it -- and they are not close, the ratio between them spreading 1.87x / 22.9x / 1831x at n = 3/6/9 (n = 3A, so n=9 is A=3). Quoting only the primary would be an overclaim. THE FR pullback redistributes within a depth stratum and preserves that stratum's total, so the redistribution rule and the base measure are two independent choices; the rule is family-agnostic and is unchanged between arms. THE TWO ARMS DISAGREE ON THE BEST KNOT, which is the whole reason for reporting both: Molien -> 5_2 (+21.4% vs its own baseline 1.5489x, with 6_1 at 1.6068x, WORSE than baseline); d_q^2/D^2 -> 6_1 (+1.7% vs its own baseline 1.0660x). The canonical arm gives the FR MECHANISM stronger support and the paper's 6_1 NAMING none. COMPARABILITY: the 1.82x baseline / 1.5015x best-4_1 figures quoted downstream are from a PRE-MIGRATION d_q^2/[n]_q! run and are NOT comparable with either arm here. FULL FAMILY SURVEY (bean qou-oots, same harness): d_q^2/[n]_q! -> 4_1 best; d_q^2/D^2 -> 6_1; Molien -> 5_2; y_lambda -> vacuous (SU(N) row cap zeroes depth >= 2). So no k=3 knot conclusion from this producer is interpretable without naming the family it was computed under. SCOPE: this is the FR-VARIANCE route. The corpus's structural 6_1 naming at curvature-rank 3 comes from the GB-filtration route (prop:curvature-rank-gb-stratification), which carries no weight family at all and is untouched by any of the above. Braid words sourced from _deprecated/hyperbolic_knot_db_extended.py canonical table.",
